🔹 Product Vision: Task Management + Time Tracking

An application that allows individuals and organizations to manage their tasks, projects, and timesheets in a professional, streamlined way.

Think of it as:

Jira-style task management → structured projects, sprints, workflows, assignments, status tracking.

Notion-style notes & flexibility → documentation, personal notes, customizable task views.

Timesheet tracking → employees or freelancers can log hours against tasks/projects.

🔹 Core Features
1. Task Management

Create, assign, and track tasks

Support for projects, boards, and lists (Kanban, Scrum, To-do, etc.)

Task attributes: title, description, tags, assignee, due date, priority

Custom workflows (like Jira’s status columns)

2. Collaboration & Documentation

Rich text editor (Notion-style) for task descriptions and project docs

Commenting & discussion on tasks

File & image attachments

Mentions (@employee) and notifications

3. Time Tracking & Timesheets

Employees can log hours per task/project

Automatic or manual timers

Weekly & monthly timesheet views

Export reports (CSV/PDF) for payroll or invoicing

4. Dashboards & Analytics

Project progress (burn-down charts, task completion rate)

Employee productivity reports

Time spent by task/project/client

5. User & Role Management

Teams, departments, clients

Roles: Admin, Manager, Employee, Client

Permissions: who can edit/view tasks or reports

🔹 Advanced (Optional for v2)

AI assistant → auto-generate tasks from notes/meetings

Calendar integration (Google/Outlook)

Slack/Teams integration for task updates

Mobile app for quick updates on-the-go

🔹 Tech Stack (Recommended)

Since you’re already working with React + Node.js/Nest.js + MySQL/MongoDB, a good stack could be:

Frontend: Next.js (React + Tailwind + ShadCN for UI)

Backend: Nest.js (TypeScript, scalable APIs)

Database: PostgreSQL/MySQL (for structured data)

Auth: JWT / OAuth2 (Google, Microsoft login)

File Storage: S3 bucket (for attachments)

Deployment: Docker + Vercel (frontend) + AWS/GCP (backend)

🔹 MVP (Minimum Viable Product)

To start lean, focus on:

Task creation & assignment

Project boards (Kanban view)

Timesheet logging (manual)

Dashboard with task & time overview